{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 10,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.308,
            0.089,
            0.441,
            0.105
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Example 9.1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.306,
            0.105,
            0.9,
            0.156
          ],
          "content": "**A convex mirror used for rear-view on an automobile has a radius of curvature of 3.00 m. If a bus is located at 5.00 m from this mirror, find the position, nature and size of the image.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.164,
            0.397,
            0.18
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Solution"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.308,
            0.181,
            0.618,
            0.198
          ],
          "content": "**Radius of curvature,** $R = + \\: 3 . 0 0$ **m;**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.308,
            0.198,
            0.617,
            0.215
          ],
          "content": "**Object-distance, u = – 5.00 m;**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.308,
            0.215,
            0.546,
            0.231
          ],
          "content": "**Image-distance,** $v = 2$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.308,
            0.231,
            0.546,
            0.248
          ],
          "content": "Height of the image, $h ^ { \\prime }   = 2$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.308,
            0.254,
            0.9,
            0.307
          ],
          "content": "Focal length, $f = R / 2 = + \\frac{3.00   m }{2} = + 1.50$ <strong><u>m</u></strong> (as the principal focus of **a convex mirror is behind the mirror)**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.308,
            0.313,
            0.461,
            0.349
          ],
          "content": "**Since** ${ \\frac { 1 } { v } }   +   { \\frac { 1 } { u } } = { \\frac { 1 } { f } }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.309,
            0.356,
            0.748,
            0.443
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{1}{v}=\\frac{1}{f}-\\frac{1}{u}=+\\frac{1}{1.50}-\\frac{1}{(-5.00)}=\\frac{1}{1.50}+\\frac{1}{5.00}",
          "image_source": "images/page_10_equation_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.308,
            0.45,
            0.511,
            0.484
          ],
          "content": "v = \\frac{+7.50}{6.50} = +1.15   m",
          "image_source": "images/page_10_equation_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.486,
            0.713,
            0.504
          ],
          "content": "**The image is 1.15 m at the back of the mirror.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.508,
            0.674,
            0.567
          ],
          "content": "**Magnification,** $m = \\frac{h'}{h} = - \\frac{v}{u} = - \\frac{1.15   m }{-5.00   m }$ **=** + 0.23"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.306,
            0.567,
            0.875,
            0.585
          ],
          "content": "**The image is virtual, erect and smaller in size by a factor of 0.23.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.602,
            0.441,
            0.618
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Example 9.2"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.306,
            0.618,
            0.899,
            0.686
          ],
          "content": "**An object, 4.0 cm in size, is placed at 25.0 cm in front of a concave mirror of focal length 15.0 cm. At what distance from the mirror should a screen be placed in order to obtain a sharp image? Find the nature and the size of the image.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.308,
            0.692,
            0.397,
            0.708
          ],
          "content": "**Solution**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.308,
            0.709,
            0.541,
            0.725
          ],
          "content": "Object-size, $h = + 4.0\\  cm ;$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.308,
            0.726,
            0.586,
            0.742
          ],
          "content": "Object-distance, $u = - 25.0\\  cm ;$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.308,
            0.742,
            0.547,
            0.759
          ],
          "content": "Focal length, $f = -15.0    cm ;$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.308,
            0.76,
            0.514,
            0.775
          ],
          "content": "Image-distance, $v = 2$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.308,
            0.776,
            0.469,
            0.792
          ],
          "content": "Image-size, $h ^ { \\prime }   = 2$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.308,
            0.792,
            0.458,
            0.809
          ],
          "content": "**From Eq. (10.1):**"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.318,
            0.815,
            0.414,
            0.851
          ],
          "content": "{ \\frac { 1 } { v } } + { \\frac { 1 } { u } } = { \\frac { 1 } { f } }",
          "image_source": "images/page_10_equation_23.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.861,
            0.731,
            0.897
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{1}{v}=\\frac{1}{f}-\\frac{1}{u}=\\frac{1}{-15.0}-\\frac{1}{-25.0}=-\\frac{1}{15.0}+\\frac{1}{25.0}",
          "image_source": "images/page_10_equation_24.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
